I'll follow an EMNLP-style format but keep it simple. Rather than trying to embed actual image files, I'll use text-based descriptions and tables to present the results, focusing on clear exposition of the methods and findings.\n\nNow I'm ready to write the paper itself, making sure to pull all the numerical results directly from the experiment data and follow the style guidelines around avoiding em-dashes, gerunds, and AI-specific language. I'll organize it as an abstract, introduction, background and methods section, experimental setup, results, and discussion, aiming for a honest presentation of what the experiments actually showed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2823,"cache_read_input_tokens":37322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2823},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbfb10b1-9baa-4831-b283-8555e0a1834a","uuid":"865eb1c3-9dd9-4a73-81c4-80d61968fa2b"}
